# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Secrets -- never commit these. backend/.env currently holds a live
# GROQ_API_KEY; keeping it out of git from the start (this repo has no prior
# history) means it never ends up in a commit that would need to be scrubbed
# later. Copy frontend/.env.example -> frontend/.env locally if you need one
# there too; that pattern stays untracked the same way.
**/.env
!**/.env.example

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Python (backend)
backend/venv/
**/__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.pytest_cache/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Node (frontend) -- frontend/.gitignore already covers these for that
# folder; repeated here so the root file is self-sufficient too.
frontend/node_modules/
frontend/dist/
frontend/dist-ssr/
*.local
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
pnpm-debug.log*

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Editor / OS
.vscode/*
!.vscode/extensions.json
.idea/
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*.suo
*.ntvs*
*.njsproj
*.sln
*.sw?

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Application runtime data (generated, not source code).
#
# backend/app/data/companies/ is this app's live per-company database --
# project registries, Phase 1 records, Phase 3 baselines, logged bills, and
# background-job results (backend/app/services/company_store.py). It's
# mutable state that grows every time someone uses the app, it contains real
# client project data (e.g. "Ecopolitan"), and some of these result files run
# multiple MB each -- none of which belongs in source control. The static
# reference datasets that ship WITH the app (cea_baseline/, ice_db/,
# reference_boqs/, work_orders/, canonical_material_categories.json) are
# deliberately NOT matched by this rule and stay tracked as normal.
backend/app/data/companies/
backend/app/data/companies_registry.json

# Root-level sample/uploaded documents (real Certificate-of-Payment bill
# PDFs) -- same reasoning: real project documents, not source code.
/data/
